{
  "scope": "CPU-only diagnostic lazy butterfly and fused twist kernels; production NTT methods are unchanged. A friend declaration permits diagnostics to reuse the original immutable root/twist tables.",
  "initial_kernel_commit": "6086b89",
  "arithmetic": "For p<2^30, DIF maintains residues below2p with a sum reduction modulo2p; its differences are below4p. Multiplying a value below4p by a canonical Montgomery twiddle gives t<4p^2<p*2^32, hence REDC below2p. DIT reduces the even input below2p, permits its odd input below4p, and produces values below4p. Untwisting restores canonical outputs. The terminal SIMD DIF stage canonicalizes its input before producing canonical spectrum values.",
  "short_stages": "SIMD8/4 stages keep lazy residues and the final2 stage canonicalizes, avoiding a separate normalization pass before short stages. Scalar fallback uses the same proved bounds.",
  "fused_variant": "Fuse twisting into the first DIF butterfly and untwisting into the last DIT butterfly, eliminating two standalone array passes while preserving the same field operations and bounds.",
  "unit_coverage": "AVX2 and scalar x86-64/no-AVX2 builds each pass1088 cases: all17 distinct RNS primes, sizes2..65536, both short-stage policies and natural/bit-reversed ordering. Check intermediate2p/4p ranges and final canonical values, compare spectra and inverse transforms on arbitrary inputs with the existing kernels, and compare small-ring forward evaluation and negacyclic convolution with independent integer formulas. Fused bit-reversed transforms additionally match the original spectrum, arbitrary-spectrum inverse and round trip. No keys or encryption are involved.",
